<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!-- MuseConfig SAMPLE — placeholders only. NEVER ship this file as-is
	     and NEVER put a real key, secret, or token in it.
	     SETUP (developer, before shipping):
	       1. Copy this file to MuseConfig.plist (same folder) and add the
	          COPY to the app target (target > Build Phases > Copy Bundle
	          Resources). The sample itself must not be bundled: the app
	          loads only MuseConfig.plist, and MuseConfig.load() rejects
	          every placeholder value below, so an unedited copy fails
	          closed with a "not configured" error instead of connecting.
	       2. Replace every PLACEHOLDER value with real values from YOUR
	          Meta developer dashboard, and VERIFY each one there before
	          shipping: the Model API base URL, the OAuth client ID, the
	          redirect URI, the scopes, and the model ID.
	       3. Do NOT commit a filled-in MuseConfig.plist with real values
	          to any shared repository: the client ID is not a password,
	          but the configuration still belongs to your developer
	          account. Tokens are never stored here — they live only in
	          the macOS Keychain (see Services/MuseAuthService.swift).
	     HONEST-DESIGN NOTE: the following are ONLY third-party-reported
	     defaults, noted so you have a starting point to check — verify in
	     your Meta developer dashboard before shipping; they are NOT
	     Meta-confirmed facts and they are NOT active defaults anywhere
	     in code (the active values below are placeholders that fail
	     closed):
	       third-party-reported base URL: https://api.meta.ai/v1
	       third-party-reported model: muse-spark-1.3
	     The authorize/token paths are derived from the base URL with
	     conventional OAuth2 paths (see MuseConfig.swift); verify those
	     paths in your Meta developer dashboard too. FileRadar is not
	     affiliated with or endorsed by Meta. -->
	<key>MuseBaseURL</key>
	<string>YOUR_MODEL_API_BASE_URL</string>
	<key>MuseClientID</key>
	<string>YOUR_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID</string>
	<key>MuseRedirectURI</key>
	<string>fileradar://muse-callback</string>
	<key>MuseScopes</key>
	<array>
		<string>YOUR_SCOPE_1</string>
	</array>
	<key>MuseModel</key>
	<string>YOUR_MODEL_ID</string>
</dict>
</plist>
